{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Walk before.</b> [This corresponds to] etc. — a letter heh was added to his name, making it complete and whole for the count of 248 limbs in a person. And likewise it is concluded at the end of the fourth chapter of Nedarim: Rami bar Rabbi Abba said — it is written אברם and it is written אברהם. At first the Holy One, blessed be He, made him sovereign over 243 limbs, and ultimately over 248. And these are: two eyes, two ears, and the head of the male organ. Come and see how great is the power of circumcision, as is stated in the fourth chapter of Nedarim. And it was stated in the Mekhilta: why does Scripture not call Avraham and Sarah by their names after they were changed, as we find with Ya'akov, who was called Ya'akov after the Holy One, blessed be He, called him Yisra'el? Because the first name of Avraham and Sarah was not uprooted entirely, but only one letter of heh was added to their name. And since it was a correction of the name, once the correction took effect the original was submerged. But with Ya'akov, a new name was given to him, and the first name did not depart from its place. And further they said: for this reason the name of Yitzchak was not changed — because no name was ever given to him except from the mouth of the Almighty, as it is said: ״וקראת את שמו יצחק״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:30.749260800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}